<title>UK: UK's Labour's will not put VAT on food.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour's will not put VAT on food.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The opposition Labour Party economics spokesman Gordon Brown on Thursday repeated a pledge not to extend the scope of VAT to include transport, food, children's clothes and books and newspapers if the party wins the May 1 eleciton.</p>
<p>But Brown refused to be drawn on what a Labour government's policy on VAT on other areas would be.</p>
<p>Brown was speaking at a news conference called to criticise the government's increase of VAT on fuel and to repeat Labour's pledge to cut the tax on heating to five percent from eight percent.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
